# Patch 0005 — skill: a review message may carry only accept and reject decisions, with no thread id
# Offered back: yes
# Files: skill/SKILL.md
#
# Reason: the skill describes every `[obsidian-diff]` message as carrying a thread id to reply
# into. A host that batches a reviewer's decisions (romp sends the accepts and rejects made since
# the last message as one message per file) can send a message with no comment at all — the
# person went over the file, accepted or rejected the pending changes, and left nothing to
# answer. An agent reading such a message by the old description would look for a thread id
# that is not there. One sentence says the shape exists and that nothing needs a reply. Pinned
# by the drift test only (prose).
diff --git a/skill/SKILL.md b/skill/SKILL.md
index e9a9bb60..8a8c4394 100644
--- a/skill/SKILL.md
+++ b/skill/SKILL.md
@@ -125,7 +125,10 @@ for the file named here":
 - **`[obsidian-diff]`** — a review-panel ping about a change or a comment: the file
   by ABSOLUTE path, the reviewer's message, and a THREAD id. One message may list
   several comments on the same file, each with its own thread id; address each one
-  and reply into each by its own id.
+  and reply into each by its own id. A message may also carry only the reviewer's
+  accept and reject decisions on your earlier changes, with no comment and so no
+  thread id to reply into: nothing needs an answer, and the file already reads as
+  decided.
 
